{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Or it shall gore a son, or it shall gore a daughter</b> — He said \"or\" as an addition, and its full phrasing is <b>and it shall kill a man or a woman, or it shall gore a son or it shall gore a daughter</b> — one law applies to all of them. And some say that it comes in place of \"if\" (Radak in Sefer haShorashim, root או; and so Rashi on Leviticus 4:23). And similarly: <b>or from the carcass of an unclean beast</b> (Leviticus 5:2), <b>or I have dealt falsely with my life</b> (II Samuel 18:13), <b>or it is known that it is a goring ox</b> (Exodus 21:36), and so many others according to their opinion. All of them are false witnesses — you will understand them in their places.<br>And Scripture needed to spell out the law of minors, according to the opinion of our Rabbis of blessed memory (Bava Kamma 44a), because above (Exodus 21:29) it needed to say \"a man or a woman\" to teach that it equated a woman to a man for all damages in the Torah, and one might think he would be liable only for grown men and women — therefore it states <b>or it shall gore a son</b> to impose liability for minors just as for adults. And Scripture did likewise with <b>And if a man strikes any human being</b> (Leviticus 24:17), as Rashi writes there. And according to the plain sense, it is because an ox that kills a grown person is very evil, like a vicious dog in the wilderness, and if <b>it has been warned by its owners and they did not guard it</b>, this is a very great negligence and it is fitting that its owner should be liable for death and ransom, but one that kills minors is not so evil, for it is the way of most oxen not to fear them, and it would occur to one's mind that its owner should not be liable. Therefore Scripture said that <b>according to this judgment shall it be done to it</b>."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:13:52.861373249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}